=== Upgrades ===
There are 5 '''Composter Upgrades''' available for the Composter.
* Composter Speed (requires {{Skl|Garden|2}}): Increases Composter production speed by {{Green|20%}} per tier. The maximum speed is {{Green|+500%}}, or {{Green|6x}}. Without the Multi Drop upgrade, each tier of this upgrade increases the Composter's production rate by 1.2 Compost per hour, worth about {{BZC|*1.2 Compost}} before accounting for Multi Drop.
* Multi Drop (requires {{Skl|Garden|4}}): When Compost is produced, grants a {{Green|3%}} chance per tier to produce an extra one. The maximum chance is {{Green|75%}}. Without the Composter Speed upgrade, each tier of this upgrade increases the Composter's production rate by 0.18 Compost per hour on average, worth about {{BZC|*0.18 Compost}}.
* Fuel Cap (requires {{Skl|Garden|6}}): Increases the maximum [[Machine Fuel|{{DarkGreen|Machine Fuel}}]] that the Composter can hold by {{Green|30,000}} per tier. Including the base value, the maximum limit is {{Green|850,000}} [[Machine Fuel|{{DarkGreen|Machine Fuel}}]].
* Organic Matter Cap (requires {{Skl|Garden|8}}): Increases the maximum amount of {{Yellow|Organic Matter}} that can be stored by {{Green|30,000}} per tier. Including the base value, the maximum limit is {{Green|790,000}} {{Yellow|Organic Matter}}.
* Cost Reduction (requires {{Skl|Garden|10}}): Reduces the amount of {{Yellow|Organic Matter}} and [[Machine Fuel|{{DarkGreen|Machine Fuel}}]] required to produce Compost by {{Green|1%}} per tier. The maximum reduction is {{Green|25%}}, which results in the consumption of {{Green|3,000}} Organic Matter and {{Green|1,500}} [[Machine Fuel]] per Compost.

A Composter with all Composter Upgrades maxed out would produce an average of {{Item|Compost|amount=63}} per hour. For each hour, it would consume {{Green|108,000}} {{Yellow|Organic Matter}} and {{Green|54,000}} [[Machine Fuel|{{DarkGreen|Machine Fuel}}]]. It could run unattended for exactly 5 hours before running out of {{Yellow|Organic Matter}}, making an average of {{Item|Compost|amount=315}} in that time. Even with the {{yellow|Organic Matter Cap}} upgrade maxed out, the first 6 upgrades of the {{darkGreen|Fuel Cap}} are enough for the {{yellow|Organic Matter}} to be depleted fully.
